   "definition_quote": "In the decoupled bandits, the learner selects an arm $i_t \\in [K]$ to exploit, and an arm $j_t \\in [K]$ to explore at each round $t\\in [T]$, which may be the same or different. Then, the learner suffers $\\ell_{t,i_t}$ without observing it, and observes $\\ell_{t,j_t}$ without suffering it. ... In the adversarial regime, loss vectors are determined by an adaptive adversary, in response to the learner's past actions."
  },
